{
  "abstract": "We study sub-quadruple regular extensions of two-sided rational Diophantine quintuples, proving that the regular fifths are linear in a + b and cut out the Branch 1 sextuple surface and two twin-fifth surfaces. Factoring the four-tuple regularity relation on regular fifths defines a two-dimensional surface that collapses on Branch 1 to a smooth genus-three curve of relation type (5, 2), yielding an unramified descent and a new rational almost septuple satisfying 20 of 21 square conditions. We construct explicit parametric sextuple families, moving-parameter quintuple families on an elliptic curve with a 2-adic period-6 lock, and a universal triple-square section of the five-tuple regularity polynomial with a rank-2 Mordell-Weil sublattice. In symmetric sub-quadruple coordinates, we prove a universal One-R5 Lorentz Norm Identity, establish the algebraic splitting of the compatibility locus into two bilinear factor loci, formulate the plus-branch birational correspondence, and reduce the core norm polynomial from 875 terms to 449 terms via a Dual Brahmagupta Identity with explicit genus-0 rational curves (including an all-positive quintuple) and a bidegree-(2,2) physical terminal-root equation that reduces to a genus-0 conic in (xi, (xi-1)uv) and a 219-term polynomial in (R, D_br, tau). For the central five-tuple relation, we prove a generic four-factor norm decomposition into two-term binomials with automatic square discriminants and a rank-at-least-one elliptic family of two-sided quintuples. Finally, on the three-torsion K3 base and paired/antipodal sextuple sources, we establish Master Syzygies, a Chebyshev elliptic fibration with positive 22/28 octuple sections, 2-Selmer/Chabauty closures, and exchange-quotient conic syzygies. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 18 incorporating the Central-R5 two-term binomial decomposition and rank-at-least-one elliptic family E_{13,2} (exp46) and the Universal Lorentz Norm Identity, Dual Brahmagupta reduction, explicit c != 0 genus-0 curves C_{rat,1}(r), C_{rat,2}(m), and Physical Terminal-Root Equation Q_phys = 0 (exp47), while addressing all reviewer items from the Version 17 acceptance report (mS_0IwRZi4lq8KMb) and the Version 18 review (3wYq5xcv4Kg1Bf4u), verified in verify_paper.py (exp9-exp47) and THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md (Theorem 21(4)-(6)) in supplement.zip: (1) Corrected defining F_1(m), F_2(m) formulas on E_{13,2} (Reviewer Item 1 of 3wYq5xcv4Kg1Bf4u, Theorem 4(1)(d), Theorem 21(5), and exp46): Proved and directly verified against the defining extension expressions that on E_{13,2} (r(m) = (m^2-2)/(2m), Y_2(m) = (m^2+2)/(2m)), F_1(m) = (m^2-2)^2 C_1(m^2) / (4 m^2 (m^2-4)(m^2-1)^2) and F_2(m) = C_2(m^2) / (m^2 (m^2-4)) (matching F_1(6) = -1198483/88200 and F_2(6) = 1157/72 at m = 6), so F_i(m) = square iff (m^2-4) C_i(m^2) = square, and matched the abstract rank-at-least-one wording to the certified lower bound; (2) Corrected bidegree-(2,2) characterization of Q_phys and proved its (xi, zeta = (xi-1)s_2) genus-0 conic reduction and 219-term M_core(R, D_br, tau) elimination (Reviewer Item 2 of 3wYq5xcv4Kg1Bf4u, Theorem 4(1)(c), Theorem 21(6), and exp47): Explicitly proved and checked in exp47 that Q_phys : 4 R W_num (xi^2 - 1) - (L_Y xi + L_X)^2 = 0 (xi = X_1/D) has bidegree (2,2) in (s_2, xi) with leading s_2^2-coefficient -(D_br + 2)^2 (xi - 1)^2, and under the birational blow-up zeta = (xi - 1) s_2 transforms into a total-degree-2 genus-0 conic in (xi, zeta), parameterized rationally via L_Y xi + L_X = 2 R (1 + D_br tau)(xi + 1) to reduce the common-root resultant with the base quintuple quadratic to a 219-term polynomial M_core(R, D_br, tau) = 0 of tridegree (8,6,8); (3) Universal Lorentz Norm Identity, Dual Brahmagupta Reduction (449-term N_core), explicit c != 0 genus-0 curves C_{rat,1}(r), C_{rat,2}(m) (all-positive quintuple {99/7, 16/63, 133/144, 637/16, 459/112} at m=3), and all 3 polish items from mS_0IwRZi4lq8KMb.",
